  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3743",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Kcnc3 and Kcnv2, both of which are involved in the same biological process—Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Kcna7, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Guanidine may influence Kcna7 through the modulation of potassium channel function. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, biologically plausible relationship, with Guanidine acting as a modulator of potassium channel activity, which is a well-documented mechanism in cellular physiology. The shared involvement of Kcnc3 and Kcnv2 in the same pathway further supports the idea that Guanidine may target a common regulatory node in the potassium channel network, potentially affecting Kcna7 through a direct or indirect interaction. The evidence suggests that Guanidine could modulate Kcna7's function by influencing the activity of its associated potassium channels, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
